From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: keep the application's pNext chain when adding present scaling

win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR adds VkSwapchainPresentScalingCreateInfoEXT when the swapchain extent
differs from the window (DPI virtualization, display mode change emulation), but it replaces the
whole pNext chain with it. The application's structures are lost: DXVK creates swapchains with
VK_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT_KHR and a VkImageFormatListCreateInfo, and Mesa's
wsi_configure_image then dereferences the missing format list (NULL + 16), so every D3D game that
changes the display mode (3DMark 11 at 1280x720) crashes in vkCreateSwapchainKHR. Chain the scaling
structure in front of the application's instead. Present in upstream Wine 11.22 too.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
index 58dba2e0..6653e16f 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -1861,6 +1861,10 @@ static VkResult win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR( VkDevice client_device, const VkSwa
         physical_device->extensions.has_VK_KHR_swapchain_maintenance1)
     {
         scaling.scalingBehavior = VK_PRESENT_SCALING_STRETCH_BIT_EXT;
+        /* Chain it in front of the application's structures instead of replacing them: dropping
+         * e.g. VkImageFormatListCreateInfo while VK_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT_KHR is set
+         * (as DXVK does) crashes drivers that rely on it (Mesa's wsi_configure_image). */
+        scaling.pNext = create_info_host.pNext;
         create_info_host.pNext = &scaling;
     }
 
